==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|positive|ly|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|pŏzʹĭtĭvli}}, {{IPA|/ˈpɒzɪtɪvli/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-positively.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|manner}}&nbsp; In a [[positive]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|He approached the interview '''positively'''.}}
# {{lb|en|modal}}&nbsp; With [[certainty]].
#: {{ux|en|I will '''positively''' be there at 8 a.m.}}
# {{lb|en|degree}}&nbsp; [[very|Very]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1963|author={{w|Margery Allingham}}
|title={{w|The China Governess}}
|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL2004261W
|passage=The half-dozen pieces […] were painted white and carved with festoons of flowers, birds and cupids. [&hellip;]&nbsp; The bed was the most extravagant piece.&nbsp; Its graceful cane halftester rose high towards the cornice and was so festooned in carved white wood that the effect was '''positively''' insecure, as if the great couch were trimmed with icing sugar.}}
#: {{ux|en|I had a '''positively''' wonderful time.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|with certainty}} {{l|en|definitely}}, {{l|en|categorically}}, {{l|en|decisively}}, {{l|en|unconditionally}}

